<title>USA: FOB Gulf Grain - Wheat basis little changed.</title>
<headline>FOB Gulf Grain - Wheat basis little changed.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>FOB hard red and soft red winter wheat basis levels remained little changed on Monday, despite news that Egypt had bought supplies from Australia, Argentina and France rather than the U.S.</p>
<p>There was also talk Pakistan may soon be seeking Australian wheat amid sentiment that U.S. wheat is overpriced. Tight supplies helped to underpin values.</p>
<p>&quot;There is just not a lot of wheat around to buy,&quot; one wheat FOB broker said.</p>
<p>Soybeans values were steady, underpinned by the continued strong export pace, while corn also remained little changed.  </p>
